// Real habitat backdrop photo -- the actual "S1: Photo" image fill from the
// Figma source file (Frame 1 Desktop, node 25556:1099: a drone/photogrammetry
// scan of a river bend with a topographic contour overlay, the same asset
// the design references for this screen), not a licensed stock photo and not
// fabricated. Downloaded via the Figma MCP, re-encoded to a smaller JPEG
// (~1000px wide, quality ~72) since the original upload is a 6MB+ PNG --
// this backdrop sits fully behind the frame's own darkening scrim/grain in
// ScreenExample.svelte, so the fine detail buys nothing at full resolution.
// Embedded as a data URI (rather than a plain asset path) because svelte-package
// only copies files verbatim -- a CSS url() to a relative path would resolve
// against the *document* once Svelte injects this component's <style> at
// runtime, not against the component's own source directory, and would 404
// in the viewer even though it resolves fine in Storybook (which serves
// source directly). A data URI has no such base-path ambiguity.
export const habitatPhoto = "data:image/jpeg;base64,";
